## 2. FIVEPA'S CORE MARKETPLACE MODEL

FivePA combines a Fiverr-style predefined Gig marketplace with a PeoplePerHour-style Project marketplace and persistent buyer–seller WorkStreams.

The platform has two distinct ways to begin work.

### A. Gigs

A Gig is a predefined service published by a seller. Buyers can discover a Gig and purchase it at the seller's advertised price.

A Gig purchase creates a new Order and a new WorkStream, and funds the Order's escrow as part of the purchase process.

### B. Projects

A Project is a buyer-published opportunity to hire freelancers.

Freelancers submit Proposals. Submitting a Proposal alone does not create an Order, fund escrow, or start a WorkStream. Hiring happens when the buyer accepts the Proposal and completes the required payment/funding step.

The same Project may support multiple independent freelancer engagements while it remains open for hiring. Each hired freelancer has an independent engagement, financial record, Order, and WorkStream.

### C. WorkStreams

A WorkStream represents an ongoing buyer–seller working relationship for a particular engagement, not a permanent global relationship identified only by buyer ID and seller ID.

The same buyer and seller may have multiple WorkStreams, including separate WorkStreams for separate Gig purchases.

An existing WorkStream can also support continued communication, follow-on Proposals, and additional work where the buyer and seller choose to continue their relationship there.

**An Order ending does not mean the WorkStream must end.**

Completed or cancelled Orders do not automatically terminate the WorkStream, remove its chat history, prohibit new Proposals, or prohibit repeat business.

