## 3. USERS, ACCOUNTS, AND MARKETPLACE FREEDOM

### 3.1 Buyers and sellers

The marketplace must allow users to buy services and offer services under the existing account and authorization rules.

Do not introduce a rule that permanently assigns a user to only one role when the existing implementation permits both buyer and seller activity.

Do not introduce arbitrary restrictions on the number of Gigs, Projects, Proposals, WorkStreams, repeat engagements, or legitimate conversations.

In particular, sellers must not be given a newly imposed maximum number of active or published Gigs. FivePA's intended marketplace model permits sellers to publish an unlimited number of Gigs, subject to existing technical and legitimate safety controls.

### 3.2 Account status and security

Authentication, authorization, account status, and financial permissions must be enforced correctly.

Security controls should prevent unauthorized actions without creating unrelated restrictions.

Where an account is restricted, suspended, frozen, or deactivated, follow the existing status policy for the specific action. Do not treat all account statuses as interchangeable, and do not invent additional account penalties.

Do not silently grant privileged roles, change account ownership, or permit unauthorized profile, password, email, or financial changes.

Password changes and session invalidation must protect the affected account without preventing the user from authenticating again normally.

The existing three-device session limit is intentional. Do not increase or decrease it as part of an unrelated fix.

